	doi = {10.1007/s11613-022-00781-4},
	abstract = {Theories reduce the complexity of reality and can thus serve as important orientation for consultants in their practical actions. This is illustrated with the help of three theories from motivation and social psychology, which can be used to understand the process of goal striving in coaching, to shape the relationship between coach and coachee, and to support the coachee’s self-management competencies. What is important here is an evidence-based application of theories and an openness in the counseling process. Parallels between research and consulting processes are discussed.},
