	abstract = {The paper seeks to explore pedagogical tools within flexible learning that could contribute positively to the development of skill sets for students in the context of higher education. To this effect, a systematic review was adopted in obtaining all possible studies related to flexible learning and pedagogical tools analysed and presented accordingly for this paper. A systematic review is an objective, reproducible approach to finding answers to the overarching question of this paper. There is a growing body of knowledge relating to pedagogical tools within flexible learning in higher education. In the field of learning and teaching, a well-conducted systematic review ({SR}) is considered a feasible approach to keeping academics abreast of the current evidence-based teaching and learning practice. To ensure data quality and accuracy two reviewers were engaged in the review process.},
