	abstract = {With a programmatic intention, the article frames the field of a critical educational theory of post-digital subjectivity. Based on post-digital paradigms and the subsequent assumption that a specific decision-making power is inscribed in digital media, the genuinely subject-theoretical concepts of autonomy and alienation are questioned and reinterpreted. In this way, the contours of a critical theory of education can be developed that analytically combines the theoretical questioning of the subject and practical attempts at subjective liberation.},
